Sponsored by the Re-Is-A-Little-Scared-Fuck Foundation.<br /> <br /> *If I could guarentee a more regular output of content, you'd bet your ass I'd have a Patreon for booze funds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T07:26:54-07:00","id":1310974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1310906#post1310906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your favorite writer is sober, check to see how you can sauce them up today.*<br /> <br /> This PSA is Sponsored by the Re-Is-A-Little-Scared-Fuck Foundation.<br /> <br /> *If I could guarentee a more regular output of content, you'd bet your ass I'd have a Patreon for booze funds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, in terms of Egyptian sun gods, we could do worse than Ra. We could pick Khepri, for example, and have our sun god be a giant cockroach which, by way of implication, means the life giving rays of the sun are actually a giant ball of wadded up shit.<br /> <br /> You wanna know the real curse of Mummy: the Curse. The compelling way it keeps referencing lovecraftian horror will inevitably inspire people (e.g. ME) to go out and read some of that horror, even though I know intellectually that H.P. Lovecraft was a racist, hack writer whose main skill was reusing a lot of nonsense words over and over to create the illusion of a shared universe and making his fiction seem larger and more important than it actually was. My favorite story of his is called the Unnammable, not because of the shit story but because in the opening lines he inserts himself into the story as a writer of weird fiction debating with a friend about the merits of his stories, and inflicts a self burn by having his friend call out how much of his writing involves weak willed characters going nuts by seeing things that are always indescribable and terrible for vague reasons. Even Lovecraft knew he sucked.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T08:09:23-07:00","id":1310982,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the rant, btw. Just recently got through Call of Cthulhu again, and had a hard time getting past the whole &quot;all those dirty fareigneers and not whites will kill ya if ya find out aboot their evil psychic fishy god cause they're all secretly working together and doing gross non-New English things in the shadows!!!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T09:31:21-07:00","id":1311002,"title":"","content":"No, I hear ya, that rant is always worth having.<br /> <br /> And within normal Egyptian mythos, yeah, Ra's not bad. But in Dreams of Avarice, it's presented and footnoted how the Iremites actually had little respect for the sun. This somewhat mirrors the fact that the earliest Egyptian religion was more cthonic based than solar based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T11:50:35-07:00","id":1311024,"title":"","content":"It would probably have helped to keep the rant on track. The racism on it's own is enough, the literary criticism is either just wrong, poorly researched or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T14:27:07-07:00","id":1311056,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://srconstantin.wordpress.com/2016/10/20/ra/\" target=\"_blank\">Ra can't be a scary formless god-monster you say?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T15:28:04-07:00","id":1311072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1311056#post1311056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://srconstantin.wordpress.com/2016/10/20/ra/\" target=\"_blank\">Ra can't be a scary formless god-monster you say?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting ideas, but I keep coming back to the notion that the author is talking more about Amun-Ra, or maybe just Amun period, in his concept. I think the stuff about generic excellence and all that works for Ra, as does the desire for authority for authority's sake. But all that about keeping your personal tastes secret and that being blandly mysterious is the best way to be? I dunno, maybe I lack imagination, but that speaks far more to me of Amun- THE HIDDEN ONE than it does to the big shiny sweltering disk in the sky in and of itself. Ra in the myths can definitely be cruel- like refusing to allow Geb and Nut to give birth to their children for fear they might challenge his authority. And I kinda get that if you look directly into the sun you'll go blind. But still, bright and shiny just doesn't mesh well with secrets and the man behind the man to me...least not on its own.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm biased. Amun has a lot of Lovecraftian potential in my mind, being one of the Ogdoad (e.g.- the primordial pre-creation gods of infinity, darkness, the ocean of unformed existence...and the hidden and unknown. The fact that he later pops up as deity supreme of the New Kingdom and that his cult is a big part of why the Egyptian empire fell apart also doesn't hurt.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T17:51:39-07:00","id":1311464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1311072#post1311072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting ideas, but I keep coming back to the notion that the author is talking more about Amun-Ra, or maybe just Amun period, in his concept. I think the stuff about generic excellence and all that works for Ra, as does the desire for authority for authority's sake. But all that about keeping your personal tastes secret and that being blandly mysterious is the best way to be? I dunno, maybe I lack imagination, but that speaks far more to me of Amun- THE HIDDEN ONE than it does to the big shiny sweltering disk in the sky in and of itself. Ra in the myths can definitely be cruel- like refusing to allow Geb and Nut to give birth to their children for fear they might challenge his authority. And I kinda get that if you look directly into the sun you'll go blind. But still, bright and shiny just doesn't mesh well with secrets and the man behind the man to me...least not on its own.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm biased. Amun has a lot of Lovecraftian potential in my mind, being one of the Ogdoad (e.g.- the primordial pre-creation gods of infinity, darkness, the ocean of unformed existence...and the hidden and unknown. The fact that he later pops up as deity supreme of the New Kingdom and that his cult is a big part of why the Egyptian empire fell apart also doesn't hurt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Contagion spoilers:<br /> I'd just like to note that I had that opinion about Amun well before the Edinburgh article on Contagion came out. Want that down for posterity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T20:00:47-07:00","id":1311483,"title":"","content":"Where\u2019s Irem Sobek?<br /> <br /> My Catgirl Waifu","signature":"","edited":