iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1311817#post1311817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as the teacher of kids with learning disabilities, including those on the spectrum, and as someone who has LDs (albeit not on the spectrum), I would take an extreme amount of umbrage with that description. <br /> <br /> Do. Not. Do. That.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy jeez- that was not what I spelled at all!<br /> <br /> I completely apologize, I didn\u2019t even realize my phone auto corrected my sentence: I meant to put Atrocious. Again I am very sorry Second. Thank you for bringing it to my attention!<br /> <br /> This touch screen is super finicky...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T12:19:22-07:00","id":1311834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1311824#post1311824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't get to take credit for this. I have always been like this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to see you read the part where I stated that my joking aside, you did a great job with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T12:32:03-07:00","id":1311838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1311834#post1311834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad to see you read the part where I stated that my joking aside, you did a great job with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like you. I shouldn't even be able to read you. It bothers me that I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T12:44:55-07:00","id":1311842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1311838#post1311838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like you. I shouldn't even be able to read you. It bothers me that I can.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that\u2019s fine, it doesn\u2019t upset me in the slightest. I don\u2019t like you either,<br /> but I can appreciate your talent as a writer - I don\u2019t need to be your buddy to find something that you write to be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T20:56:00-07:00","id":1311971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1311842#post1311842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that\u2019s fine, it doesn\u2019t upset me in the slightest. I don\u2019t like you either,<br /> but I can appreciate your talent as a writer - I don\u2019t need to be your buddy to find something that you write to be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>A brief lesson on social graces from an autistic person who knows how phone autocorrect works:<br /> <br /> When somebody makes a very transparent statement that you are on their Ignore List on these forums where the Ignore List condenses threads as though they did not contain posts by anyone on the list, it is rude to continue to try to interact with them in a way that flaunts the basic boundary of &quot;I don't want to talk to you and have given the forum software instructions to cut your posts out of any threads I read,&quot; particularly when that transparent statement was couched in an explicit statement that being made to interact with you via software error is an unwelcome state of affairs.<br /> <br /> Respect for personal boundaries is foundational to polite interaction. Your compliments do not outweigh a deficit of that respect if they are at all supposed to be for the person they're addressed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T05:51:35-07:00","id":1312062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1311971#post1311971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A brief lesson on social graces from an autistic person who knows how phone autocorrect works:<br /> <br /> When somebody makes a very transparent statement that you are on their Ignore List on these forums where the Ignore List condenses threads as though they did not contain posts by anyone on the list, it is rude to continue to try to interact with them in a way that flaunts the basic boundary of &quot;I don't want to talk to you and have given the forum software instructions to cut your posts out of any threads I read,&quot; particularly when that transparent statement was couched in an explicit statement that being made to interact with you via software error is an unwelcome state of affairs.<br /> <br /> Respect for personal boundaries is foundational to polite interaction. Your compliments do not outweigh a deficit of that respect if they are at all supposed to be for the person they're addressed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>To begin with, the former was apologized for as it was a honestly stupid mistake on an old and very irritating phone. I am never ashamed to admit if I make a mistake or apologize for it - you have followed me long enough to know this. Our very first serious conversation ever involved me being almost embarrassingly apologetic to you after all.<br /> <br /> And I will be honest, any lesson from you is often misguided and unnecessary due<br /> to some misplaced sense of moral obligation or a well meaning attempt to mediate over a situation that is hampered by a lack of understanding on the point you are trying to get across.<br /> <br /> Let me be perfectly blunt as I rarely get to be so: this has nothing to do with you. You do not speak for ArcaneArts in any way, unless you are Sean himself. Now unless I am mistaken; You are not his parent, nor his spouse/ significant other, or any type of person who might have some authority to speak on his behalf on any matter. He\u2019s an adult who can talk to me and work this out on his own. <br /> <br /> Not liking me is fine, I understand that, but since I had no idea that he had me on a ignore list, it is very presumptive to assume that I will know what\u2019s happening on his side of the screen, especially since I have never been given a message requesting that I stop responding to him. If he ever does that, I will be the first to apologize and aquiesce to all his requests to ignore him/ leave him be, and go my separate way. Passive aggressive, snide comments aren\u2019t going to do anything but make the other party hurt, or pissed.<br /> <br /> So do not ever demand that I show respect to someone\u2019s boundaries if they are going to be consistently hostile and rude to me in response to simply quoting them. Respect is a two way street, and should ever just be given if it isn\u2019t reciprocated. So unless you are going to lay into him for being rude as well, this post tells me that you are either unaware of what mutual respect really means, or you are defending a person that you simply like compared to me, or you honestly don\u2019t actually care about what you are saying and are just stroking your own ego behind a false sense of moral and social superiority. <br /> <br /> And if that is the case, I will ask you to stay out of this and go on your way, because clearly you are a hypocrite who doesn\u2019t practice what he preaches.<br /> <br /> But if you actually have good intentions, I understand and apologize to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-14-2019, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T08:33:51-07:00","id":1312100,"title":"","content":"Let's close this line of conversation. It's not conducive to jokes about a cruel and uncaring cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T09:18:37-07:00","id":1312106,"title":"","content":"Agreed<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s talk about how that time Ammut got drunk and thought a falcon and a bull would make cute babies together, so she called up the Shan\u2019Iatu of the Shell and said \u201c Hey... ever wanted to see what a Tweetie Beef Noodle looks like? I got the deets right here!\u201d, to which they responded with<br /> <br /> \u201c Uh, no?\u201d<br /> <br /> To which Ammut said: \u201c You sure? They shit viagra!\u201d<br /> <br /> At that revelation the Shan\u2019Iatu said: \u201c ... Go on\u201d<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s how Furaffinity started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-14-2019, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T16:19:52-07:00","id":1312179,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m a Furry to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T18:31:29-07:00","id":1312207,"title":"","content":"Welp, since I can see the response now, two things.<br /> <br /> 1) I've told Korogra several times over he's ignored. I can't help it if he doesn't remember me telling him.<br /> <br /> 2) Satchel and I hang out enough that basically you can trust him to have the measure of my opinion. I'm not saying he always speaks for me, but you can generally trust that we're in alignment unless one or the other of us clarifies otherwise (and odds are Satchel is right in those instances). And besides, he doesn't need to be speaking for me to call out someone being an asshole. Point is, if someone needs me to say that Satchel had the right of it above hand, here's me saying it. They shouldn't, though, because the saliency of his commentary doesn't need my rubber stamp, or anyone else's for that matter.<br /> <br /> Anyways, something something furries something something don't jam your clam with Amkhata?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-14-2019, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T19:35:09-07:00","id":1312213,"title":"","content":"I am now putting some idle thought into how portrayals of Bast and Sobek might be of use for the gameplay and narrative of Curse. Arguably every god brought up in the game so far have had bearing on the existence of the Arisen, like with how Khepera relates to kepher and such.<br /> <br /> (Maybe not Liquidity and Aridity, though I'll admit, <i>those</i> are entities I want to know more about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T20:53:56-07:00","id":1312228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1312213#post1312213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am now putting some idle thought into how portrayals of Bast and Sobek might be of use for the gameplay and narrative of Curse. Arguably every god brought up in the game so far have had bearing on the existence of the Arisen, like with how Khepera relates to kepher and such.<br /> <br /> (Maybe not Liquidity and Aridity, though I'll admit, <i>those</i> are entities I want to know more about.)</div> </div> </div> </div>As they factor hard into my worship, I\u2019d love to see the messy mythical overlap where Bast-Sekhmet-Hathor are sort of all the same goddess sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T21:41:06-07:00","id":1312234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1312228#post1312228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As they factor hard into my worship, I\u2019d love to see the messy mythical overlap where Bast-Sekhmet-Hathor are sort of all the same goddess sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is a place to play around with that, it'd be Curse. Honestly, there's probably a pre-Naquada interpretation begging for use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T23:26:35-07:00","id":1312248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1312234#post1312234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is a place to play around with that, it'd be Curse. Honestly, there's probably a pre-Naquada interpretation begging for use.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s something distinctly Curse about the idea of domesticating a feral war goddess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T02:49:19-07:00","id":1312264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1312213#post1312213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am now putting some idle thought into how portrayals of Bast and Sobek might be of use for the gameplay and narrative of Curse. Arguably every god brought up in the game so far have had bearing on the existence of the Arisen, like with how Khepera relates to kepher and such.<br /> <br /> (Maybe not Liquidity and Aridity, though I'll admit, <i>those</i> are entities I want to know more about.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think interesting questions get raised, considering the animal associations with each of the Guilds, as well as the visual appearances of Arisen when they're using some of their transformational powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T11:26:00-07:00","id":1312347,"title":"","content":"Since Ra was considered the Nameless Lion at that time, I suspect Bast and company may tie into him via the Eye of Ra myth. basically, he was convinced or tricked to bestow his power on another entity and promptly drove it insane. Maybe by insights seen on the Scroll of Ages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T11:51:56-07:00","id":1312356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1312248#post1312248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There\u2019s something distinctly Curse about the idea of domesticating a feral war goddess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah Bastet was a savage War goddess before becoming a motherly Hawt cat girl. kind of like how Set was a Good guy before Egypt got invaded. Set was the God of <span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><b>Foreigners</b></span></span> and to add insult to injury the new ruling class got really in to Set worship. <br /> <br /> i do not know how and why Bastet got tamed do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T12:14:06-07:00","id":1312367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1312356#post1312356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i do not know how and why Bastet got tamed do</div> </div> </div> </div>...Because somebody wanted their hawt catgirl waifu?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T12:38:05-07:00","id":1312377,"title":"","content":"I've actually toyed with the concept of Sobek in M:tC as a force of balance of some sort- a circle of creation and destruction which devours civilizations to bring allow new ones to grow. Some kind of &quot;anti Ammut&quot; in the respect that it brings death to fertilize life, and grow life in order to feed death, a manifestation of the dual Rivers which Sutekh cried as he lost his eyes.<br /> <br /> Probably shares a few aspects with Apocalypse's Wyrm, even though I haven't thought about it while writing the homebrew on the subject. Either it was subconsciously, or that it is just a commonly used theme *shrugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T18:43:54-07:00","id":1331424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history?p=1312248#post1312248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There\u2019s something distinctly Curse about the idea of domesticating a feral war goddess.</div> </div> </div> </div> Metaphor for the conquest of Egypt by the Greeks, one of it's great War Lion Goddess defenders gets domesticated and erotized, symbolizing the taming of Egypt, while Sekmet remains focused on War, Symboling Egypt can never be tamed completely.<br /> <br /> Not sure how this applies to Irem exactly, but it popped into my head.<br /> <br /> Sobek is mentioned in DE2.<br /> <br /> Maybe in Iremite Mythology they could end up tied to the lore of Immortals or Minor Guilds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user"